package cajeta.aot;

/**
 * Declares a factory class — one method per provided type, for the cases
 * @Component construction cannot cover: third-party/unowned types, assisted
 * (caller-supplied, non-@Inject) arguments, and initialization beyond the
 * constructor (AspectModel.md § @Factory, rules R1–R4).
 *
 * R1: resolution keys on the method SIGNATURE (return type = provided type;
 *     @Inject params = dependency edges) — the body is arbitrary.
 * R2: the method returns a freshly heap-allocated owned `#T`; the framework
 *     owns caching/drop per the declared scope (the body must not self-cache).
 * R3: @Inject params are graph-resolved; unmarked params are assisted. Any
 *     assisted param ⇒ consumers inject the FACTORY and call it; all-injected
 *     ⇒ it is a provider and consumers inject the PRODUCT.
 * R4: scope is declared on the method ({@link Singleton} / {@link Transient}).
 */
annotation Factory {
}
